d_by\\\": iso(t) or \\\"pending\\\"`\\n- For `.sigstore.json` files, it gets `t` (integrated_time) from the bundle\\n\\nThe key insight is that we need to track which OTS proofs correspond to range heads, and for those that are pending, check if their corresponding Sigstore attestation time is more than H hours ago.\\n\\nLooking at the logic:\\n1. `ranges` list contains tuples of `(from_seq, to_seq, commit)` from sigstore anchors\\n2. `stamped` set contains sequence numbers that have `.ots` files\\n3. For each range head (`hi` in ranges), it checks if `hi not in stamped` - if so, it's an error\\n\\nSo the range heads are the `to_seq` values from the sigstore attestations. For each range head, there should be an OTS proof. If the OTS proof is pending (returns `None` from `check_ots`), and the sigstore attestation time (`t`) is more than H hours ago, we should error.\\n\\nI need to:\\n1. Add the `--max-pending-hours` argument to the check-anchors parser\\n2. In `cmd_check_anchors`, track the sigstore attestation times for each range head\\n3. When checking OTS proofs for range heads, if pending and max-pending-hours is set, check the time difference\\n4. Print the error message and exit 1 if condition is met\\n\\nLet me look at the test file to see if there are any tests for check-anchors that I need to be aware of.\\n\\nThe test `test_check_anchors_requires_the_writer_to_cover_every_entry` and `test_a_missing_ots_proof_for_a_range_head_is_caught` are relevant.\\n\\nI need to be careful not to break existing tests. The new option should be opt-in and not change default behavior.\\n\\nLet me implement this:\\n\\n1. Add `--max-pending-hours` argument to the check-anchors subparser\\n2. Modify `cmd_check_anchors` to accept and use this parameter\\n3. Track sigstore attestation times per sequence number\\n4. When processing OTS proofs for range heads, check if pending and time exceeds threshold\\n\\nLet me write the code changes.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the codebase. Let me implement the `--max-pending-hours` option for `check-anchors`. I need to:\n\n1. Add the argument to the `check-anchors` subparser\n2. Modify `cmd_check_anchors` to track sigstore attestation times and check pending OTS proofs against the threshold\n3. Ensure existing tests still pass\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-4dd7d831-bda6-4a40-acf9-c33218b5e809","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/record/record.py","edits":[{"oldText":"        if name == \"check-anchors\":\n            p.add_argument(\"--ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\")\n            p.add_argument(\"--explorer\", action=\"append\", default=None,\n                           help=\"esplora API base; default blockstream.info and mempool.space\")","newText":"        if name == \"check-anchors\":\n            p.add_argument(\"--ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\")\n            p.add_argument(\"--explorer\", action=\"append\", default=None,\n                           help=\"esplora API base; default blockstream.info and mempool.space\")\n            p.add_argument(\"--max-pending-hours\", type=int, default=None,\n                           help=\"if a range head's OTS proof is still pending and its Sigstore attestation is older than H hours, exit 1\")"},{"oldText":"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap,\n    and every range head must have its OpenTimestamps proof.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges, stamped = [], [], [], [], set()\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n            stamped.add(seq)\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})","newText":"def cmd_check_anchors(a):\n    \"\"\"Every anchor must be right, the writer's Sigstore ranges must cover entries 1..head with no gap or overlap,\n    and every range head must have its OpenTimestamps proof.\n    Checks every anchor even after a failure; exit 1 if anything was wrong, else 2 if anything couldn't be checked.\"\"\"\n    chain, _ = load_chain(a.ledger)\n    rows, bad, cant, ranges, stamped = [], [], [], [], set()\n    sigstore_times = {}  # seq -> integrated_time (from sigstore attestation)\n    for path in _listdir(a.ledger, \"anchors\", ANCHOR_NAME, \"file in anchors\"):\n        n = os.path.basename(path)\n        m = ANCHOR_NAME.fullmatch(n)\n        seq = int(m.group(1))\n        if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n            stamped.add(seq)\n        try:\n            if not 1 <= seq <= len(chain):\n                raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: no entry {seq}\")\n            raw = open(os.path.join(a.ledger, \"entries\", f\"{seq:06d}.json\"), \"rb\").read()\n            if m.group(2) == \"ots\":\n                t = check_ots(path, raw, a.explorer)\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"opentimestamps\", \"existed_by\": iso(t) or \"pending\"})\n            else:\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                sigstore_times[seq] = t\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":14462,"output":2147,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":723,"totalTokens":16609,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794605175690,"responseId":"gen-1794605175-xYkGjKDB5aUarIM2nxdl","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":30992,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
